# Screenshots

This folder contains screenshots captured during different stages of the RTL-to-GDSII implementation flow.

The images include floorplanning, power planning, placement, clock tree synthesis, routing, physical verification, and the final GDSII layout.

The screenshots provide a visual representation of the complete ASIC Physical Design flow implemented using Cadence Innovus.
# Screenshots

The following screenshots highlight the important stages of the RTL-to-GDSII implementation flow.

## 1. Floorplan + Power Planning
Core area definition along with VDD and VSS power rings and stripes.

![Floorplan](screenshots/01_floorplan_global.png)

---

## 2. Placement – Global View
Standard cells placed across the core with optimized utilization and zero routing overflow.

![Placement Global](screenshots/02_placement_global.png)

---

## 3. Placement – Zoomed View
Zoomed view showing standard cell instances and placement quality.

![Placement Zoomed](screenshots/03_placement_zoomed.png)

---

## 4. Clock Tree Synthesis (CTS)
Balanced clock tree generated using CCOpt for minimum skew and optimized latency.

![Clock Tree](screenshots/04_cts_clock_tree.png)

---

## 5. Post-CTS Timing Results
Timing summary after setup and hold optimization.

![Post CTS Timing](screenshots/05_postcts_timing.png)

---

## 6. Routed Layout – Global View
Final routed design showing metal interconnections across the entire layout.

![Routing Global](screenshots/06_routing_global.png)

---

## 7. Routed Layout – Zoomed View
Detailed routing view showing metal layers and via connections.

![Routing Zoomed](screenshots/07_routing_zoomed.png)

---

## 8. Physical Verification Summary
Verification reports confirming zero DRC violations, zero connectivity violations, and zero PG shorts.

![Verification](screenshots/08_verification_summary.png)

---

## 9. Final GDSII Layout
Final layout exported as a GDSII stream file after successful timing closure and signoff verification.

![Final GDSII](screenshots/09_final_gdsii.png)
